# olympus.conf — optional; copy to the repo root.
# PARSED as whitelisted key=value lines, never shell-sourced: nothing here is executed
# at load time (repo write access must not equal shell execution — bin/README security
# line). Unknown keys are ignored with a warning. AGENT_CMD's value IS a command, but
# it runs only inside heartbeat's hard wall-clock budget.
# Everything commented out = that channel stays off. Hands keep working regardless.

# Command used for unattended heartbeat runs. Unset ⇒ heartbeat only reports & notifies.
# heartbeat enforces a hard wall-clock timeout around this command regardless of its flags;
# a turn bound in the command itself is the second belt (doctor flags its absence).
#AGENT_CMD="claude -p --max-turns 30 --permission-mode acceptEdits"
# Codex seat equivalent (resume keeps the thread's warm context; name = stable handle):
#AGENT_CMD="codex exec --sandbox workspace-write"

# Hard wall-clock budget per unattended run, minutes (default 15).
#HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_MIN=15
# Grace added to decision `due:` before the fallback must be applied, minutes (default 30).
#OLYMPUS_FALLBACK_GRACE_MIN=30

# Where `notify` posts. ntfy: one curl = one phone push. Lark: incoming-webhook URL.
#NTFY_TOPIC="https://ntfy.sh/<your-private-topic>"
#LARK_WEBHOOK="https://open.larksuite.com/open-apis/bot/v2/hook/<token>"

# Per-seat wake channel, read by `bin/olympus wake <handle>`:
#   local            → run `heartbeat <handle>` on this machine, in the background
#   https://…        → POST that URL (e.g. a Claude Code Routine fire endpoint)
#   notify (default) → just tell the humans via NTFY/LARK above
# ONE WAKE HOME PER SEAT: exactly one automatic executor per seat, declared here once.
# Do not point a cron on machine A and a CI heartbeat at the same seat — the extra
# channel must be `notify`. (bin/README "One wake home per seat".)
#WAKE_zeus="local"
#WAKE_athena="https://api.example/routines/<id>/fire"
